1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,242
Today's topic: Anime Pilgrimage—Visiting Sacred Anime Locations!

2
00:00:08,242 --> 00:00:11,242
Scene 1: Anime Pilgrimage: Your Name

3
00:00:11,242 --> 00:00:18,809
Our anime pilgrimage journey begins today!

4
00:00:18,832 --> 00:00:22,380
Yes, I'm so excited!

5
00:00:22,403 --> 00:00:25,670
Where are we heading first?

6
00:00:25,694 --> 00:00:33,254
Suga Shrine in Yotsuya—the iconic spot from *Your Name*.

7
00:00:33,277 --> 00:00:39,743
Ah, the famous red staircase shrine!

8
00:00:39,766 --> 00:00:42,565
That's the one.

9
00:00:42,589 --> 00:00:47,256
It's where the two main characters first meet—a really special place.

10
00:00:47,279 --> 00:00:51,816
How long is the walk from the station?

11
00:00:51,839 --> 00:00:55,739
Just about 10 minutes on foot.

12
00:00:55,762 --> 00:00:59,732
Good thing the weather's nice today.

13
00:00:59,756 --> 00:01:02,656
Oh, I see it!

14
00:01:02,679 --> 00:01:05,712
That staircase, right?

15
00:01:05,735 --> 00:01:12,118
Wow, it looks *exactly* like in the movie!

16
00:01:12,142 --> 00:01:15,409
It really does!

17
00:01:15,431 --> 00:01:20,698
Look—there are so many foreigners taking photos here.

18
00:01:20,721 --> 00:01:25,788
Let's take a picture from the same angle as the movie!

19
00:01:25,811 --> 00:01:28,144
Great idea!

20
00:01:28,167 --> 00:01:32,438
You go up the stairs.

21
00:01:32,462 --> 00:01:34,995
Got it!

22
00:01:35,018 --> 00:01:39,252
I'll stay down here and look up.

23
00:01:39,275 --> 00:01:43,073
Okay, I'm taking the photo now!

24
00:01:43,096 --> 00:01:48,269
Say cheese!

25
00:01:48,292 --> 00:01:51,276
Did it turn out well?

26
00:01:51,299 --> 00:01:56,166
Yes, it's a perfect shot!

27
00:01:56,189 --> 00:01:59,822
It looks just like the movie poster!

28
00:01:59,845 --> 00:02:02,822
I'm so happy!

29
00:02:02,846 --> 00:02:08,079
There are more interesting spots nearby, too.

30
00:02:08,102 --> 00:02:10,896
Like what?

31
00:02:10,919 --> 00:02:16,086
The intersection and mailbox from the movie are just around here.

32
00:02:16,109 --> 00:02:20,342
Oh, I want to see those too!

33
00:02:20,365 --> 00:02:22,865
Let's go together!

34
00:02:22,888 --> 00:02:26,355
Sure, let's check them out!

35
00:02:26,378 --> 00:02:30,411
After this, we'll head to the next pilgrimage site.

36
00:02:30,434 --> 00:02:33,146
Got it!

37
00:02:33,170 --> 00:02:35,870
Where are we going next?

38
00:02:35,893 --> 00:02:41,593
Kanda Shrine near Akihabara.

39
00:02:41,616 --> 00:02:48,721
Check the description and top comment for a link to review today's video! *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

40
00:02:48,721 --> 00:02:51,721
Scene 2: Exploring Akihabara and Kanda Shrine

41
00:02:51,721 --> 00:02:56,878
We've arrived near Akihabara!

42
00:02:56,901 --> 00:03:02,375
Walking through Electric Town is always so fun.

43
00:03:02,398 --> 00:03:10,745
Today, we're visiting Kanda Shrine—a famous anime pilgrimage spot.

44
00:03:10,768 --> 00:03:17,002
Kanda Shrine is really old, isn't it?

45
00:03:17,025 --> 00:03:19,858
Yes, it is.

46
00:03:19,881 --> 00:03:26,867
This is where the anime idols trained every day.

47
00:03:26,891 --> 00:03:32,624
You mean the long staircase inside the shrine?

48
00:03:32,647 --> 00:03:36,147
That's the one.

49
00:03:36,170 --> 00:03:41,303
That's the *Otoko-zaka* (Men's Slope) staircase.

50
00:03:41,326 --> 00:03:45,093
Ah, this is it!

51
00:03:45,116 --> 00:03:51,029
It's steeper and taller than I expected!

52
00:03:51,053 --> 00:03:57,686
In the anime, the characters would run up these stairs!

53
00:03:57,709 --> 00:04:01,443
That's amazing!

54
00:04:01,466 --> 00:04:06,848
I feel tired just from walking.

55
00:04:06,871 --> 00:04:12,904
Let's take it slow and walk up together.

56
00:04:12,927 --> 00:04:15,664
Yes, it is.

57
00:04:15,687 --> 00:04:19,205
Let's climb one step at a time.

58
00:04:19,229 --> 00:04:23,495
We made it to the top!

59
00:04:23,518 --> 00:04:26,864
The view is beautiful, isn't it?

60
00:04:26,888 --> 00:04:34,022
There are so many anime ema (wooden plaques) inside the shrine!

61
00:04:34,045 --> 00:04:40,745
Fans draw pictures and write their wishes on them.

62
00:04:40,767 --> 00:04:46,122
You can really feel the love from fans all over the world.

63
00:04:46,146 --> 00:04:52,296
There are also cute omamori (charms) inside the shrine.

64
00:04:52,320 --> 00:04:56,953
Are those anime character charms?

65
00:04:56,976 --> 00:05:02,410
Yes, they're special collaboration charms.

66
00:05:02,432 --> 00:05:07,132
Those would make great souvenirs.

67
00:05:07,155 --> 00:05:10,655
I want to buy one too!

68
00:05:10,678 --> 00:05:14,993
Then let's head to the shop.

69
00:05:15,017 --> 00:05:20,117
Tomorrow, we're heading to the seaside!

70
00:05:20,140 --> 00:05:23,473
Wow, the ocean?

71
00:05:23,496 --> 00:05:27,329
I'm so excited!

72
00:05:27,352 --> 00:05:36,338
Comment when you figure out the answer!

73
00:05:36,338 --> 00:05:39,338
Scene 3: Kamakura’s Sacred Spot – The Famous Railroad Crossing

74
00:05:39,338 --> 00:05:45,872
We took the Enoshima Electric Railway and arrived in Kamakura!

75
00:05:45,894 --> 00:05:51,930
The blue ocean from the train was so beautiful.

76
00:05:51,953 --> 00:06:00,299
This is the sacred spot from a basketball anime—famous worldwide!

77
00:06:00,323 --> 00:06:05,002
It's the Kamakura High School crossing, right?

78
00:06:05,025 --> 00:06:08,059
That's the one.

79
00:06:08,082 --> 00:06:13,315
The crossing where the main character stands in the opening.

80
00:06:13,338 --> 00:06:18,716
Oh, look—so many people are gathered over there!

81
00:06:18,740 --> 00:06:24,407
Everyone's waiting for the green train to pass.

82
00:06:24,430 --> 00:06:32,330
It's popular because you can see the ocean, the crossing, and the train all at once.

83
00:06:32,353 --> 00:06:38,086
We have to take a photo as soon as the train comes!

84
00:06:38,109 --> 00:06:41,661
When is the train arriving?

85
00:06:41,685 --> 00:06:46,385
It should be here in about two minutes.

86
00:06:46,408 --> 00:06:49,841
Get your camera ready!

87
00:06:49,864 --> 00:06:52,532
Got it!

88
00:06:52,556 --> 00:06:55,789
I'm getting nervous!

89
00:06:55,812 --> 00:07:00,646
Oh, I hear the *clang clang* sound!

90
00:07:00,669 --> 00:07:03,635
The train is coming!

91
00:07:03,658 --> 00:07:08,168
Here comes the beautiful green train!

92
00:07:08,192 --> 00:07:10,658
Taking the photo now!

93
00:07:10,681 --> 00:07:14,592
Did you get a good shot?

94
00:07:14,616 --> 00:07:16,794
Yes, it is.

95
00:07:16,817 --> 00:07:20,851
I got the train and the ocean perfectly!

96
00:07:20,874 --> 00:07:23,707
This is incredible!

97
00:07:23,730 --> 00:07:26,563
I'm so glad!

98
00:07:26,586 --> 00:07:31,820
Should we grab something tasty nearby?

99
00:07:31,843 --> 00:07:35,076
What's famous around here?

100
00:07:35,099 --> 00:07:40,966
Shirasu don (rice bowl with tiny whitebait) is really famous!

101
00:07:40,989 --> 00:07:44,889
Wow, a seafood rice bowl!

102
00:07:44,912 --> 00:07:48,056
I definitely want to try it!

103
00:07:48,079 --> 00:07:52,418
Then let's find a good place to eat.

104
00:07:52,441 --> 00:07:54,635
Sure!

105
00:07:54,659 --> 00:07:57,725
I'm getting hungry.

106
00:07:57,748 --> 00:08:00,748
Scene 4: Hakone’s Hot Springs and the Setting of a Mecha Anime

107
00:08:00,748 --> 00:08:07,627
We've arrived at Hakone, a famous hot spring destination in Kanagawa Prefecture!

108
00:08:07,651 --> 00:08:15,087
There are so many mountains here—the scenery is totally different from Tokyo!

109
00:08:15,110 --> 00:08:21,077
This place was the setting for a robot anime.

110
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:27,667
Yep, this is the Third New Town from the movies and anime.

111
00:08:27,690 --> 00:08:35,556
Today, we're taking the ropeway to Owakudani.

112
00:08:35,579 --> 00:08:40,313
What can we see at Owakudani?

113
00:08:40,336 --> 00:08:47,715
White smoke billowing from the mountains—it's incredibly dramatic!

114
00:08:47,738 --> 00:08:52,455
Oh, the ropeway is starting to move!

115
00:08:52,478 --> 00:08:56,220
Check out the view from up here!

116
00:08:56,244 --> 00:09:00,344
It looks just like a scene from the anime!

117
00:09:00,367 --> 00:09:03,316
It really does!

118
00:09:03,339 --> 00:09:08,491
It's a little scary, but amazing.

119
00:09:08,514 --> 00:09:15,833
When we get to Owakudani, there's something you absolutely have to try.

120
00:09:15,856 --> 00:09:18,290
What is it?

121
00:09:18,313 --> 00:09:22,487
Black hard-boiled eggs.

122
00:09:22,510 --> 00:09:26,706
They say eating one adds seven years to your life.

123
00:09:26,729 --> 00:09:30,481
Black eggs?

124
00:09:30,505 --> 00:09:33,572
That's so cool!

125
00:09:33,595 --> 00:09:39,674
The anime characters ate them here too, you know.

126
00:09:39,698 --> 00:09:44,635
Then I *have* to try one!

127
00:09:44,658 --> 00:09:49,768
Look at all the people lined up at the shop!

128
00:09:49,791 --> 00:09:52,758
Let's get in line together.

129
00:09:52,781 --> 00:09:55,053
Yes, it is.

130
00:09:55,076 --> 00:10:00,459
After that, we can relax in the hot springs.

131
00:10:00,482 --> 00:10:03,053
Great idea!

132
00:10:03,077 --> 00:10:06,915
That should melt all the travel fatigue away.

133
00:10:06,939 --> 00:10:09,939
Scene 5: Lake Motosu and Mount Fuji

134
00:10:09,939 --> 00:10:15,693
We've arrived at Lake Motosu in Yamanashi Prefecture.

135
00:10:15,716 --> 00:10:21,483
The air is so crisp, and it's so peaceful here.

136
00:10:21,507 --> 00:10:28,473
This is where the first episode of that camping anime takes place.

137
00:10:28,496 --> 00:10:32,648
Kōan Campground, right?

138
00:10:32,672 --> 00:10:35,868
That's the one.

139
00:10:35,892 --> 00:10:41,158
You can see a stunning view of Mount Fuji from here!

140
00:10:41,181 --> 00:10:45,779
Wow, you're right!

141
00:10:45,802 --> 00:10:51,536
Mount Fuji looks enormous across the lake.

142
00:10:51,559 --> 00:11:00,034
This view is the same as the one on the back of the Japanese 1,000-yen bill.

143
00:11:00,057 --> 00:11:03,291
Wait, really?

144
00:11:03,315 --> 00:11:08,822
Let me grab a 1,000-yen bill from my wallet and check.

145
00:11:08,845 --> 00:11:11,396
See?

146
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:14,286
It's the same, isn't it?

147
00:11:14,309 --> 00:11:20,343
Whoa, it really is identical!

148
00:11:20,366 --> 00:11:25,199
The anime characters came here too.

149
00:11:25,222 --> 00:11:27,924
Yes, it is.

150
00:11:27,948 --> 00:11:33,745
They camped here while admiring Mount Fuji.

151
00:11:33,768 --> 00:11:39,151
Should we take a break here too?

152
00:11:39,175 --> 00:11:46,249
Let's sip some warm tea and enjoy the view of Mount Fuji.

153
00:11:46,272 --> 00:11:48,972
That sounds perfect.

154
00:11:48,995 --> 00:11:53,829
It's so quiet—it's really calming.

155
00:11:53,852 --> 00:12:00,918
I heard more people wanted to camp here after watching the anime.

156
00:12:00,941 --> 00:12:06,975
With a view this beautiful, I totally get it.

157
00:12:06,998 --> 00:12:12,264
Tomorrow, we're heading further west.

158
00:12:12,287 --> 00:12:15,521
Where to?

159
00:12:15,543 --> 00:12:22,514
We'll take the Shinkansen to a town with an old school.

160
00:12:22,538 --> 00:12:27,044
I can't wait to see what kind of school it is!

161
00:12:27,067 --> 00:12:30,067
Scene 6: Exploring the Anime Pilgrimage Site in Toyosato

162
00:12:30,067 --> 00:12:35,534
We've arrived in Toyosato, Shiga Prefecture!

163
00:12:35,557 --> 00:12:41,892
It was just a short walk from the station, but it's such a quiet and beautiful town.

164
00:12:41,915 --> 00:12:44,782
Look over there!

165
00:12:44,805 --> 00:12:51,272
That's the old elementary school building.

166
00:12:51,295 --> 00:12:58,028
Wow, it's such a grand and beautiful building!

167
00:12:58,051 --> 00:13:05,963
This is the real-life model for the school in *K-On!*, the music anime.

168
00:13:05,987 --> 00:13:12,320
It's where the Light Music Club members practiced, right?

169
00:13:12,343 --> 00:13:15,443
That's the one.

170
00:13:15,466 --> 00:13:20,566
We can go inside and take a look around!

171
00:13:20,589 --> 00:13:24,861
The guide is so friendly, isn’t she?

172
00:13:24,885 --> 00:13:31,637
Check out the rabbit and turtle decorations on the stair railings!

173
00:13:31,661 --> 00:13:36,328
Those exact decorations appear in the anime too!

174
00:13:36,351 --> 00:13:40,263
You really know your stuff!

175
00:13:40,286 --> 00:13:44,753
Let’s head up to the club room on the third floor.

176
00:13:44,776 --> 00:13:47,749
Yes, I’d love to!

177
00:13:47,773 --> 00:13:54,149
This is where they drank tea and ate snacks in the anime.

178
00:13:54,172 --> 00:14:01,672
There are desks, chairs, and even a blackboard inside the club room.

179
00:14:01,695 --> 00:14:07,196
Fans have brought instruments and teacups here too.

180
00:14:07,219 --> 00:14:13,253
It feels like we’ve stepped right into the anime—so exciting!

181
00:14:13,276 --> 00:14:18,209
You can even write a message on the blackboard!

182
00:14:18,232 --> 00:14:23,826
Then I’ll write a message in my language!

183
00:14:23,849 --> 00:14:26,549
Great idea!

184
00:14:26,572 --> 00:14:29,639
This will be a great memory.

185
00:14:29,662 --> 00:14:35,529
I’m so glad we got to see this historic school today.

186
00:14:35,552 --> 00:14:42,852
Now, let’s head to a special spot deep in the mountains next!

187
00:14:42,875 --> 00:14:46,069
Sure, let's check them out!

188
00:14:46,092 --> 00:14:49,092
Scene 7: Yagyu’s Legendary Sword-Split Rock

189
00:14:49,092 --> 00:14:56,392
We’ve come for a walk in the mountains of Yagyu, Nara Prefecture.

190
00:14:56,415 --> 00:15:02,589
It’s so green all around—nice and cool, isn’t it?

191
00:15:02,612 --> 00:15:08,846
This place is a hotspot for *Demon Slayer* fans!

192
00:15:08,869 --> 00:15:13,435
What’s in these mountains?

193
00:15:13,458 --> 00:15:17,653
There’s a huge rock here.

194
00:15:17,677 --> 00:15:22,511
It’s called the Yagyu Sword-Split Rock.

195
00:15:22,534 --> 00:15:26,267
The Yagyu Sword-Split Rock?

196
00:15:26,290 --> 00:15:29,323
What kind of rock is it?

197
00:15:29,346 --> 00:15:37,813
It looks just like the rock Tanjiro split in half with his sword!

198
00:15:37,836 --> 00:15:43,417
Ah, the rock from the final training scene!

199
00:15:43,440 --> 00:15:46,940
Oh, there it is!

200
00:15:46,963 --> 00:15:50,532
That massive rock over there.

201
00:15:50,555 --> 00:15:57,789
Wow, it’s really split clean down the middle!

202
00:15:57,812 --> 00:16:06,487
Legend says a famous swordsman from the Edo period split it while fighting a tengu.

203
00:16:06,511 --> 00:16:10,411
So it’s a legendary rock!

204
00:16:10,434 --> 00:16:15,606
No wonder it’s split so perfectly!

205
00:16:15,629 --> 00:16:20,427
There’s even a wooden sword in front of the rock!

206
00:16:20,450 --> 00:16:27,717
Can I take a photo in the main character’s pose with this?

207
00:16:27,741 --> 00:16:30,974
Of course you can!

208
00:16:30,997 --> 00:16:34,531
Get into your stance.

209
00:16:34,554 --> 00:16:37,940
Alright, here we go!

210
00:16:37,963 --> 00:16:43,557
Total concentration... Got it!

211
00:16:43,581 --> 00:16:46,914
You look so cool!

212
00:16:46,937 --> 00:16:49,637
Thank you!

213
00:16:49,660 --> 00:16:54,493
I feel like I became the anime’s main character!

214
00:16:54,516 --> 00:16:58,750
I’m glad you enjoyed it!

215
00:16:58,773 --> 00:17:02,540
The scenery around here is really beautiful, isn’t it?

216
00:17:02,564 --> 00:17:08,955
Yes, it’s so peaceful in this quiet forest—you can really feel the history.

217
00:17:08,978 --> 00:17:14,335
Alright, let’s head down the mountain and make our way to Kyoto.

218
00:17:14,359 --> 00:17:18,993
What kind of sacred sites are there in Kyoto?

219
00:17:19,015 --> 00:17:24,652
It’s the shrine that appears in that famous detective anime!

220
00:17:24,675 --> 00:17:27,675
Scene 8: Fushimi Inari and the Senbon Torii Gates

221
00:17:27,675 --> 00:17:33,148
We’ve arrived at Fushimi Inari Taisha in Kyoto.

222
00:17:33,172 --> 00:17:40,205
Look at all these red torii gates—it’s absolutely stunning!

223
00:17:40,228 --> 00:17:48,773
This place has been featured in many anime, including movies from *Detective Conan*.

224
00:17:48,797 --> 00:17:54,163
*The Crossroads of the Labyrinth*, right?

225
00:17:54,186 --> 00:17:58,053
You remember that well!

226
00:17:58,076 --> 00:18:03,383
There’s a scene where they walk through this tunnel of torii gates.

227
00:18:03,407 --> 00:18:10,195
The gates just keep going—it feels like stepping into another world.

228
00:18:10,219 --> 00:18:18,592
It’s called the Senbon Torii, though there are actually way more than a thousand!

229
00:18:18,615 --> 00:18:25,281
I heard this is the number one place foreign tourists want to visit.

230
00:18:25,304 --> 00:18:31,046
Yeah, it’s packed with people every single day.

231
00:18:31,070 --> 00:18:37,174
How long does it take to hike all the way to the top?

232
00:18:37,197 --> 00:18:43,430
If you go all the way around the mountain, it takes about two hours.

233
00:18:43,453 --> 00:18:47,420
Two hours sounds tough!

234
00:18:47,443 --> 00:18:51,551
Let’s just walk a little today.

235
00:18:51,574 --> 00:18:54,851
Sounds good.

236
00:18:54,874 --> 00:19:01,107
The light filtering through the torii gates is so beautiful.

237
00:19:01,130 --> 00:19:07,464
Yeah, no matter where you take a photo, it turns out like a painting.

238
00:19:07,487 --> 00:19:13,657
Walking while listening to the anime’s soundtrack makes it even more fun!

239
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:17,314
That’s a great idea!

240
00:19:17,338 --> 00:19:21,605
Let’s play it on our phones.

241
00:19:21,628 --> 00:19:27,494
Enjoy the atmosphere of this traditional Japanese shrine.

242
00:19:27,517 --> 00:19:34,451
Yes, I’m so glad I got to come to Kyoto.

243
00:19:34,474 --> 00:19:41,307
We walked a lot today, so let’s relax tonight.

244
00:19:41,330 --> 00:19:45,311
I’m craving something delicious!

245
00:19:45,334 --> 00:19:50,201
I’ve prepared some special Kyoto cuisine for you.

246
00:19:50,224 --> 00:19:53,939
Wow, I can’t wait!

247
00:19:53,962 --> 00:19:56,962
Scene 9: Kyoto Inn and Onsen Experience

248
00:19:56,962 --> 00:20:03,429
Tonight, we’re staying at a traditional Kyoto inn.

249
00:20:03,452 --> 00:20:08,685
The tatami room feels so calming.

250
00:20:08,708 --> 00:20:14,608
Let’s change into yukata and head to the onsen first.

251
00:20:14,631 --> 00:20:21,298
This is my first time in a Japanese onsen—I’m a little nervous.

252
00:20:21,321 --> 00:20:26,988
The water’s hot, so take your time getting in.

253
00:20:27,011 --> 00:20:31,277
Okay, I’ll be careful.

254
00:20:31,300 --> 00:20:37,634
After your bath, a delicious dinner will be waiting for you.

255
00:20:37,657 --> 00:20:42,690
Wow, is this Kyoto cuisine?

256
00:20:42,713 --> 00:20:47,425
The small, elegant plates are so pretty.

257
00:20:47,449 --> 00:20:55,016
This is *kaiseki*—it uses lots of seasonal vegetables and tofu.

258
00:20:55,039 --> 00:21:00,306
The flavors are so delicate and delicious.

259
00:21:00,329 --> 00:21:06,567
How about we look through our travel photos while we eat?

260
00:21:06,590 --> 00:21:09,161
That sounds perfect.

261
00:21:09,185 --> 00:21:13,218
Let’s check them out on our phones.

262
00:21:13,241 --> 00:21:19,992
The photo of the Yotsuya stairs at the beginning is so beautiful.

263
00:21:20,015 --> 00:21:27,648
The Kamakura High School crossing shot turned out great—the train looks perfect.

264
00:21:27,671 --> 00:21:34,771
The one with the big rock in Nara, where you’re holding a wooden sword, is hilarious.

265
00:21:34,794 --> 00:21:41,332
Every place looked just like the anime—I was so moved!

266
00:21:41,356 --> 00:21:48,075
We got to see so many beautiful sights in Japan—it was such a wonderful trip, wasn’t it?

267
00:21:48,099 --> 00:21:54,455
Yes! You’re really great at planning trips.

268
00:21:54,478 --> 00:21:57,178
Thank you.

269
00:21:57,201 --> 00:22:01,901
I’m so happy you enjoyed it.

270
00:22:01,924 --> 00:22:07,510
Tomorrow’s finally our last day of the trip.

271
00:22:07,534 --> 00:22:13,367
It’s bittersweet, but let’s make the most of our last day tomorrow!

272
00:22:13,390 --> 00:22:17,290
Yes, goodnight.

273
00:22:17,313 --> 00:22:20,313
Scene 10: Memories of Our Anime Pilgrimage Trip

274
00:22:20,313 --> 00:22:27,346
Today marks the end of our anime pilgrimage trip.

275
00:22:27,369 --> 00:22:35,145
Before heading back to Tokyo on the Shinkansen, we bought tons of souvenirs.

276
00:22:35,169 --> 00:22:41,728
Kyoto Station is such a massive and modern building, isn’t it?

277
00:22:41,752 --> 00:22:51,452
Yeah! Even though there are so many old temples around, the station itself is surprisingly new.

278
00:22:51,475 --> 00:22:58,308
Which pilgrimage site was your favorite on this trip?

279
00:22:58,331 --> 00:23:07,869
For me, it was definitely the railroad crossing by the sea in Kamakura—it was so moving.

280
00:23:07,892 --> 00:23:13,028
The ocean in Shonan was absolutely stunning.

281
00:23:13,052 --> 00:23:18,919
What about you? Which place left the biggest impression?

282
00:23:18,942 --> 00:23:28,408
I’ll never forget the huge split rock I saw in the mountains of Nara.

283
00:23:28,431 --> 00:23:36,023
That place was so peaceful—it really felt like stepping into an anime world.

284
00:23:36,046 --> 00:23:43,113
Where would you want to go for our next pilgrimage trip?

285
00:23:43,136 --> 00:23:51,036
Next time, I’d love to visit Ghibli Park or some of the film locations in Kyushu.

286
00:23:51,059 --> 00:23:53,658
Great idea!

287
00:23:53,682 --> 00:23:58,915
Kyushu has so many beautiful spots too!

288
00:23:58,938 --> 00:24:05,039
What about all of you watching? Which anime pilgrimage site is your favorite?

289
00:24:05,062 --> 00:24:09,981
Let us know in the comments!

290
00:24:10,004 --> 00:24:15,038
We’d love to hear about your favorite anime locations too.

291
00:24:15,061 --> 00:24:21,161
It’s almost time for our Shinkansen, so let’s head to the platform.

292
00:24:21,184 --> 00:24:26,284
Yes, let’s go back to Tokyo.

293
00:24:26,307 --> 00:24:31,807
We’ll see you all again in our next travel video!

294
00:24:31,830 --> 00:24:34,530
Goodbye!